{"meta":{"dataset":"opinions","title":"Legal-marketing ethics opinions, 2004–2026","version":"2.4.0","doi":"10.5281/zenodo.24383274","doiUrl":"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24383274","conceptDoi":"10.5281/zenodo.23656748","license":"CC BY 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","attribution":"Source: Probative Growth, Legal-marketing ethics opinions, 2004–2026, version 2.4.0, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24383274, licensed CC BY 4.0.","citation":"Probative Growth. (2026). Legal-marketing ethics opinions, 2004–2026 (Version 2.4.0) [Data set]. Zenodo. https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24383274","citeAs":"Probative Growth, Legal-marketing ethics opinions, 2004–2026, 2026, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24383274","disclaimer":"Not legal advice. This is a plain-English summary of public ethics opinions, kept for marketing planning, and opinions and rules change. Check with your state bar and your own counsel before you run an ad.","notice":"Probative Growth is a marketing firm, not a law firm; not legal advice.","lastChecked":"2026-11-18","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/opinions/index.json","humanUrl":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/opinions/","statusCodes":{"P":"primary source","S":"secondary source"}},"source":{"publisher":"Probative Growth","page":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/opinions/","version":"2.4.0","license":"CC BY 4.0","citeAs":"Probative Growth, Legal-marketing ethics opinions, 2004–2026, 2026, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24383274"},"summary":"An index of US state and ABA ethics opinions, committee guidelines and court rulings on lawyer advertising and marketing, from 2004 to 2026 (most from 2015 on, plus earlier landmarks): lead generators, pay-per-lead, reviews, testimonials, trade names, websites, social media, chatbots and AI tools, competitor keywords and more. Version 1.1 adds an AI sub-index: 14 AI opinions coded on six marketing questions (chatbot disclosure, AI-made ads, intake and solicitation, superiority claims, confidentiality in marketing tools, and fees). Each record gives the issuing body, number, date, topics, a one-sentence holding in our words, a practical step, whether it is still in force, the official link, an exact short quote and the date read. It is not the opinions' full text. Version 2.1 adds a table of AI guidance for lawyers by jurisdiction (ai-guidance.csv and ai-guidance.json): what official AI guidance for lawyers from 31 jurisdictions says on six marketing questions, each answer a verbatim quote with its place in the document, and 10 jurisdictions with no statewide AI guidance for lawyers in the bar's or court's ethics opinion or guidance index read on November 13, 2026.","key":"jurisdiction","count":296,"keys":[{"key":"ABA","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/opinions/jurisdictions/ABA.json","records":2},{"key":"AK","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/opinions/jurisdictions/AK.json","records":3},{"key":"AL","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/opinions/jurisdictions/AL.json","records":1},{"key":"AZ","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/opinions/jurisdictions/AZ.json","records":2},{"key":"CA","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/opinions/jurisdictions/CA.json","records":13},{"key":"CO","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/opinions/jurisdictions/CO.json","records":5},{"key":"CT","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/opinions/jurisdictions/CT.json","records":5},{"key":"DC","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/opinions/jurisdictions/DC.json","records":5},{"key":"DE","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/opinions/jurisdictions/DE.json","records":3},{"key":"FL","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/opinions/jurisdictions/FL.json","records":9},{"key":"GA","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/opinions/jurisdictions/GA.json","records":2},{"key":"HI","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/opinions/jurisdictions/HI.json","records":5},{"key":"IA","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/